g missing, nothing stubbed, no module skipped.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 41 rows. The key mechanical finding: the C has **no error protocol at all** (no sentinel, no `errno`, no `assert`, no null check, no enum). The rejection surface is guards that no-op, loop bounds that iterate zero times, the implicit `malloc`-failure path, and hard faults.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 36 rows over 9 axes, including the hidden-state axis and all 12 entry points (not just `hatch`).\n\n## Phases B–D\n\n76 differential tests, all green under 3 feature combinations × 2 build profiles. Both `.so`s are `dlopen`ed; the Rust crate is never linked directly. The harness makes the hidden state observable *and settable* through public exports only (`complex_calc(0,0,0)` reads the counter, `process_pointer_data(&v,0)` reads the accumulator), so tests are order-independent.\n\n## Two real bugs found and fixed\n\n1. **Debug assertions changed observable behaviour.** With `debug-assertions` on, rustc injects a null-deref check into the raw-pointer loads; the panic can't unwind across `extern \"C\"`, so the process died with **SIGABRT (6) where the C gives SIGSEGV (11)**. Fixed with `[profile.dev] debug-assertions = false`. This was only visible because I added a build-profile axis — the default `cargo test` run was green.\n\n2. **The suite could pass vacuously.** `cargo test` does *not* build a `cdylib`-only lib target, so a leftover `target/debug/libhatch_lib.so` was being tested while freshly rebuilt code was ignored. `rust_so_path()` now resolves deterministically and **panics with `STALE ARTIFACT`** if the `.so` predates `src/lib.rs`.\n\nI found the second bug only because `mutation_check.sh` suddenly reported five surviving mutants it had killed on the previous run — without that cross-check, the green results would have been meaningless. All 25 injected bugs are now handled correctly (23 killed; 2 proven semantically equivalent and documented as *required* survivors, e.g. relaxing `shift < num_records` to `<=` only adds a zero-byte `memmove`).\n\n## Things I deliberately did not test, and said so\n\nThread safety (a data race in *both*, so no deterministic expected result), `count` near `INT_MAX` in `compute_with_dynamic_memory` (allocator-state-dependent, not a translation property), and `DataRecord.name`/`.timestamp` written inside `hatch` (never read back before `free`). These are listed in `VERIFICATION.md` rather than quietly omitted.\n\n`c_src/` is unmodified — md5sums verified; the only addition is the prescribed `build/` directory.","ttft_ms":2909,"ttft_stream_ms":2790,"time_to_request_ms":44,"type":"result","duration_ms":2875791,"uuid":"d78649cf-fb20-4988-99ed-113ea6f1bdf7","queued_turn_count":0}
